s you the power to track  the progress on a project  with lots of moving parts  okay we've talked about starting your  document and collecting information with  others  and we talked about collaborating around  that document what does google do  to help you help you save time with the  fine-grained  copy and polish  one feature in google docs that helps  you get to that level of polish  is our default text styles feature  google docs allows you to set up custom  title and heading styles  with custom styles you get formatting  that matches your company's brand  or your own personal style this makes it  easy for you to keep that level of  polish you want  without expanding a lot of extra energy  fonts matter for polish too there are  some that are good for documents that  are read on a personal screen  while others are good for the big screen  you can choose from hundreds of fonts  provided by google slides we recently  expanded the font catalog to support 62  languages  including non-latin scripts like  cyrillic and divinagari  once you find fonts you like you can add  them to your my fonts list  once they're in this list they will be  available for quick access  in the font drop-down menu on all of  your docs files  we've found in our user research there  are three top cases  where people worry the most about the  quality of their writing  in high-stakes internal collaboration  communications  when you're drafting communications that  drive key business decisions  in external collaboration when you're  drafting a document or proposal  with the intention of sharing this  outside of your company and  when you're collaborating as a  non-native speaker when you're not the  native speaker of the official language  of your company or industry  in all these cases it's critical to  ensure that your writing is correct  we are introducing grammar suggestions  in google docs  along with a revamped interface for your  spelling and grammar review  these new features build on the existing  spell check functionality  to also highlight possible grammar  errors in your text and help you correct  them  this will help you spend less time  checking and proofreading your work  and make your writing easier to  understand  google docs uses machine learning  technology to recognize and help correct  potential grammar  grammar errors in real time when docs  detects a  possible grammar correction it will  underline it in blue to indicate you  might want to check it  you can then right click to see a  suggested correction or dismiss  the alert possible grammar errors will  also show up  when you run a spelling and grammar  check through the tools menu  these features will initially launch as  an early adopter program  another place to find polishing help is  in the add-on store  here you can find rich integrations to  help you build more powerful documents  for example you can add diagrams you  created in programs outside of g suite  like in lucidchart or you can more  easily generate bibliographies and  citations  using the easybib add-on explore the  add-on store for a variety of helpful  tools  okay so we've created the document we've  worked with our collaborators  we've gotten the approvals needed  everything's polished and buttoned up  and now we're ready to send out our work  how does google docs help you in this  phase of  creating a document  when it comes to documents in the  enterprise world security matters  when there's extra sensitive information  in a document you want to be  conservative  about what the recipients can do with  the file for example  you may give some stakeholders view-only  access  this prevents them from changing their  own access level and allowing other new  people to be able to access the file  you can also prevent downloading or  making a copy of the document  this type of protection is not possible  in a world where you attach files in an  email  for the others to download and forward  at their will  to keep your organization's information  extra safe in these situations  you can also set an expiration date for  specific user actions  by user access to files in google docs  for instance  imagine your business hires an outside  contractor for a project lasting three  months to complete that job the  contractor needs to view a document  containing confidential information  about your company you share the  document containing this information  with the contractor  give them view access only and c set  that access to expire when their  contract  does in three months now if the  contractor attempts to open the document  after the expiration date has passed  they'll be denied access  google docs strives to give you full  control over how your files are shared  and this is all done with a few clicks  and a self-explanatory user interface  with google docs all the phases of  creating a document okay  sorry google docs also gives you a  choice  on how you want to share your document  while the easiest and most common way  is to share the file natively with the  right access controls as i just  mentioned  you might want you might want to share  it in a different format  you can see here the various formats  into which you can export your final  product  without losing any formatting  with google docs all the phases of  creating a document getting started  collaborating polishing and sharing are  easier and more efficient  in this talk we've taken you through a  bunch of great google docs features  custom templates in the template gallery  developer apis to generate documents  explore  and suggested data linked charts tables  and slides that remain up to date  the quick access side panel quick  meeting notes  collaboration with comments and action  items manual or automatically suggested  suggested changes in the ability to bulk  accept or reject them  named versions and clean previews  approvals and sign-offs in google docs  or on other formats via google drive  an activity dashboard to monitor monitor  approval workflows  default text formatting and more fonts  spelling and grammar improvements  add-ons and many security features  including limited access rights  exploration and exporting  that's a lot of information to take in  if you want to learn more about google  docs  or review some of the things we've  discussed here learn more today by  visiting the g suite learning center  at the link shown on your screen okay  stay tuned for live q a  we'll be back in less than a minute  hi welcome back we've gotten a number of  questions from the audience  and now we will answer them so the first  question says that doesn't keep people  from making copies of a document though  right this refers to the security  feature where we  disable copying what that does is the  sub disables the  uh file copy entry in the menu  and therefore people cannot make copies  through that mechanism  second question can i share a document i  make in google docs  with someone without a g suite account  absolutely  when you send out a document by link  people who click on the link will be  able to see your document  a cheesy account is not necessary third  question  when i share the document can the other  person know all the previous versions  and comments this depends on how you  share the document if you share it in  view only mode the person will not see  comments  or previous versions if you share it in  edit mode then they will be able to see  those things  next how do i limit access to a document  so only people at my company  see it by default when you create a  document  you choose who can see it so  if you choose to let people outside of  the company see it then you're giving  them  explicit permission but but documents by  default are only limited to the people  you have  expressly given access to  finally can i link to a specific part of  a document absolutely one of the  features in google is the bookmark  and you can insert a bookmark at any  point in the document and then you can  link directly to that point in the  document itself  i believe that's all the questions we  have  so that's all for today please tune in  next tuesday  for the next google cloud on-air webinar  and thank you for watching  you
 

